@anon.148a832d388ba4488b38de3279afe8e7.95 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [877 x i8] }> <{ [877 x i8] c"+PAGE           Begin output at page number page of the formatted input.\0A-COLUMN         Produce multi-column output. See --column\0A\0AThe pr utility is a printing and pagination filter for text files.\0AWhen multiple input files are specified, each is read, formatted, and written to standard output.\0ABy default, the input is separated into 66-line pages, each with\0A\0A* A 5-line header with the page number, date, time, and the pathname of the file.\0A* A 5-line trailer consisting of blank lines.\0A\0AIf standard output is associated with a terminal, diagnostic messages are suppressed until the pr\0Autility has completed processing.\0A\0AWhen multiple column output is specified, text columns are of equal width.\0ABy default, text columns are separated by at least one <blank>.\0AInput lines that do not fit into a text column are truncated.\0ALines are not truncated under single column output." }>, align 1
